  "summary": {},
  "notes": [
    "Printed NET OPERATING INCOME (LOSS) FROM CURRENT OPERATIONS Total 153,129,576.05 does not equal General Fund + SEF (810,396,630.18 + 106,366,823.87 = 916,763,454.05) nor Total Available minus Total Current Operating Expenditures; transcribed as printed. The NET INCREASE line on page 2 prints the expected 916,763,454.05.",
    "Debt Service (Principal Cost) / Payment of Loan Amortization of 230,128.14 (GF) is printed, but TOTAL NON-OPERATING EXPENDITURES is blank (GF) and \"-\" (Total), and NET INCREASE/(DECREASE) IN FUNDS equals Net Operating Income, i.e. the debt service was not deducted on the form. Transcribed as printed; the validator flags the non-operating total.",
    "Blank cells (most SEF item cells, the target column for expenditures, and all non-income receipt rows) are recorded as null; printed \"-\" as 0.",
    "Labels are kept as printed, including typos (e.g. \"TOTAL CURRENT OPERATING INCOE\", \"TOTAL INCOME RECEIPTS\" for total non-income receipts). The NTA line is printed as \"Internal Revenue Allotment\".",
    "Printed FUND/CASH BALANCE, END (GF) 2,899,223,791.92 equals Fund/Cash Available - Prior Year Payables - Continuing Appropriation MINUS the Advance Payment for RPT (1,721,445.15); with the advance payment added as labelled it would be 2,902,666,682.22. The SEF column adds it. The Total column (3,977,173,498.42) follows the GF figure. Transcribed as printed.",
    "This quarter has no GF/SEF reconciliation table and no Total Assets line."
  ],
  "unreadable": []
